## Context

The quality floor heatmap (Figure 2b, ticket 0466) shows claude-haiku-4.5
as all-green because `exp1_cross_eval.csv` only contains accuracy columns.
The mechanical coherence scorers already exist in `score_mechanical.py`:
`coherence_vocab_adherence`, `coherence_status_vocab_adherence`,
`coherence_row_atomicity` — and in `sota_cross_eval.csv` for Exp2.
They are simply not wired into the Exp1 scoring path (`score_exp1.py`).

This ticket is the minimum viable split from 0201: add column parity to
Exp1, rebuild the heatmap, confirm Haiku turns red. No contested composite
aggregation (that stays in 0201), no provenance or temporality scorers.

## Relevant files

- `src/aedist/score_exp1.py` — add coherence column outputs here
- `src/aedist/score_mechanical.py` — source scorers; already tested
- `experiments/derived/exp1_cross_eval.csv` — heatmap input CSV
- `src/aedist/plot_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.py` — rebuild after CSV update
